{"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/nishitadsouza/bellabeat-case-study-google-data-analytics?scriptVersionId=339474944\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"23cc2f03","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.00782,"end_time":"2026-08-01T10:51:25.682776","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-01T10:51:25.674956","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Bellabeat Case Study\n","\n","### Executive Summary\n","Bellabeat is a technology company that manufactures health-focused smart devices for women. The company's leadership team would like to understand how consumers use non-Bellabeat fitness trackers so that those insights can be used to improve Bellabeat's marketing strategy.\n","\n","This analysis focuses on identifying trends in Fitbit user behaviour and translating those findings into actionable recommendations for Bellabeat's Leaf wellness tracker.\n","\n","#### Data sources used\n","The data sources used in this case study are from the Fitbit Fitness Tracker. Thirty eligible Fitbit users consented to the submission of personal tracker data, including minute-level output for physical activity, steps, heart rate, and sleep monitoring. Data has been made available through Kaggle exploring smart device users' daily habits."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"dc1aec13","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-01T10:51:25.701654Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-01T10:51:25.699451Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-01T10:51:30.852988Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-01T10:51:30.851172Z"},"papermill":{"duration":5.165123,"end_time":"2026-08-01T10:51:30.855493","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-01T10:51:25.69037","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["── \u001b[1mAttaching core tidyverse pac